@startuml arp-ethernet-vs-wifi
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

box "Ethernet" #F0F8FF
participant "Host A" as EA
participant "Switch\n(dumb at L2)" as ESw
participant "Host B" as EB
end box

box "WiFi (802.11)" #FFF0F0
participant "Host A" as WA
participant "Access Point\n(security-aware L2 bridge)" as WAp
participant "Host B" as WB
end box

EA -> ESw : gratuitous ARP\n"I own 192.168.10.0"
ESw -> EB : flooded to all ports
note right of ESw : no validation - any host\ncan claim any IP

WA -> WAp : gratuitous ARP\n"I own 192.168.10.0"
WAp -> WAp : check: is 192.168.10.0\nregistered to this client's MAC?
WAp -x WB : ARP proxy / DAI drops frame\n(IP not in client's DHCP lease)
note right of WAp
  AP tracks "MAC -> owned IP" per
  associated client. Claiming an
  extra IP outside that mapping
  looks like spoofing, so it is
  filtered - MetalLB L2 VIPs never
  reach the rest of the network.
end note
@enduml
